# Babble physics (2026-11-16)
#
# One of four design reports on the babble seed (babble/seed.spw). Lens: symbolic physics, meaning laws that hold of Spw's symbols, found by experiment, and how the workbench's physical models meet interaction.
# Every count was measured in the workbench at cf41ca22 on 2026-11-16 by the scripts in babble/physics-scratch (logs beside them). Re-run before relying on one.
# Nothing here is decided. The wonders are the owner's to judge.

#>babble_physics_2026_11_16
#:journal #!babble
#:layer #!pragmatics

^"found"{
 # One claim a line. The counts are in the table; what the readers say of every line named here is in the probes.
 three_counts: "Every one of 856 pivots keeps three counts: the characters that are not spaces, the mark characters, and the wall characters. No other quantity measured is kept by all seven kinds."
 names_are_a_filter: "The names law is a selection, not a property of the moves. 118 of the 856 lines pivotsOf offers change the names as the fragment reader counts them: 69 lose one (attach 59, side 5, walls 5), 47 gain one (a mode turned into a body splits a dotted name in two) and 2 trade one. All 118 are among the 192 marked not read; the 664 read pivots keep every name because that is how read is defined (pivots.ts:260)."
 three_families: "The seven kinds are three families by what they do to the ink. Spacing and attach leave every non-space character in its order (97 of 97). Side and exchange rearrange the characters and change none (188 of 188). Mark and bond replace exactly one character (423 of 423), and a wall turn replaces the two of one pair (139 of 148; the other 9 also reorder the word's slots or move a mark that stood outside the walls)."
 one_way: "Two kinds are never undone by one pivot: a wall turn (0 of 148) and an attach (0 of 62). Bond and spacing are always undone by their own kind (105 of 105, 35 of 35); side and mark whenever the line reader read the result (102 of 102, 301 of 301); exchange in 21 of 28 read results."
 mark_orbit: "Turning one mark forward comes home in 12 on 122 of 152 orbits. The other 30 all stop where the turn writes a join mark (^ 16, @ 8, & 6) beside another mark or after a name: it is read as a bond and the fragment's move is gone, as ~*x to ~=x to ~@x."
 wall_orbit: "A wall turned the same way comes home in four on 20 of 141 orbits and in three on 14; 47 never write the starting line again and 60 lose the move. [[ba]] goes to [{ba}], [<ba>], [(ba)] and then round those three."
 sites_commute: "Two pivots at different sites of one line commute in 945 of 985 pairs of read pivots. Of the 40 that do not, 22 involve an exchange, 17 are two wall turns on one word, and 1 is an attach beside a side move."
 exclusion: "Two walls of one word do not turn independently: 17 of 18 pairs write different lines in the two orders, because a wall turns to the next pair its word does not already hold. x[a]{b} becomes x<a>(b) one way and x<b>{a} the other."
 exchange_moves_marks: "Exchange is the only kind that changes which name a mark is read on: @a*@b exchanged is b@@a*, whose fragments are b@ and a*. Every exchange exception in the commuting rows comes from that."
 side_is_lopsided: "A side move changes no character and no count (154 of 154 on every bag), and it is the kind that most changes what the readers count: parser statements unchanged in 46 of 154, spoken clauses in 58. Before to after is read by all three readers in 6 of 140; after to before in 14 of 14."
 readers_part: "The readers part by kind. Attach: the parser and the spoken reader read 62 of 62, the line reader 2. Side: the line reader alone reads 45 of 154. Walls: parser and spoken without the line reader, 51 of 148. Bond and spacing are read by all three in 123 of 140."
 degree: "The number of pivots a line has is a census of its sites: 3 for a name marked on one side, 2 for one marked on both, 3 for marks outside walls, 7 for a tight bond, 5 for a spaced one, 1 for each wall free to turn. It predicts 163 of 164 lines; @ba@ba@ba has 16 where the census says 17, two exchanges writing one line."
 no_pivots: "Of 1,644 short real lines the line reader reads 801 whole, and 157 of those have names and no pivot; 9 of the 43 seed lines have none. A name with no mark, no bond and a body of several parts has nothing to turn (day{wake, eat, sleep})."
 sheet_symmetries: "On the 13 term lines of the theory sheets, the only pivots that leave a term's quantity as it was are the two whitespace kinds: spacing 6 of 14 and attach 20 of 28. Of the other 144 pivots, 142 are refused or drop the term, and 2 exchanges across a power are read with another dimension (r_s from L to L^2·T^-1). No pivot moves a quantity to a nearby value."
 pinch_today: "A dimensionless group has measurable content today. T^2 · L^-1 · g reads 39.47579 with the pendulum written in s, m and kg; in ms, cm, g and km/min^2; and in natural units, where T reads 3.720846e+43. It holds by construction: the sheet stores every scale in SI base units (dimension.ts:48)."
 zoom_on_a_law: "The group tells a zoom that follows the law from one that does not: L times 4 with T times 2 leaves 39.47579; L times 4 alone gives 9.868948."
 derivative_today: "A derivative has measurable content today, in the library only. The period carries 1.0030 s per m for the rod and -0.1022 s per m/s^2 for g; a nudge of one uncertainty moves the period by 0.99975 and 0.99847 of what the derivative says. Scaled by value over value both are the law's exponents, 0.5 and -0.5."
 pinch_is_a_ratio: "factshift.center's canvas already measures a quick pinch as a ratio, with thresholds 0.8 and 1.25, which multiply to 1 (body-gestures.ts:41-42): a pinch is a pure number before any unit is chosen."
 floor_as_sheet: "spw.quest's floor is a damped spring whose damping is written as a ratio, 0.7 (physics.js:56, 282). Written as a sheet from its source constants, a held body (*) and a drifting one (~) have the same damping group, 0.5102041, by construction, and differ only in clock: the spring's natural periods are 410.7 ms and 1209.2 ms against a plain body's 662.3 ms, the drifting body 2.94 times slower than the held one. Those are periods of the spring, not times to rest. The sheet refuses px, so the floor's lengths cannot be written the same way."
 hosts_agree_on_two_axes: "Two hosts give marks forces with signs, and they agree on two axes: ground against ascension (factshift.center's canvas +2.4 and -2.4; spw.quest's floor 6 px and -6 px) and perspective against wonder (gather and open). They differ on what stands against potential: configuration on the canvas, value on the floor."
 dial_is_the_lexer_order: "The seed's dial is the order of the lexer's OperatorKind union (token.ts:17), written again in act-chains.spw:16. Six other orders of all twelve are written in the theory surfaces and on spw.quest; none keeps more than 2 of the dial's 6 half-turn pairs a half turn apart."
 label_counts: "Prior art holds most label counts: a label makes a class, so two pairs of one kind with one label nest and never cross ({_A a {_A b }_A c }_A; pair-label-reading wip.spw:57), and crossings are counted pair by pair (pair-labels.test.ts:234-248), which gives n(n-1)/2 for n pairs that all cross (run here for n from 2 to 8). What the babble needed tested: a crossing counts overlapping spans, not events, so two streams with six interleaved events have one."
 wall_turn_unmakes_a_label: "Of 20 pivots of four labeled lines, 16 keep the pairs and crossings and 4 do not. All 4 are wall turns, which write the labeled body as a concept the label scan does not read (loop<_A ~again ^_A>_A has 0 pairs)."
 labeled_lines_unread: "No labeled line probed here is read whole by the line reader: each stops at the label after a close and leaves the rest as text. The parser reads them with 0 errors, and for pairs of one brace kind the spoken reader says each close by its label, crossed or not."
 ocean_is_prose: "The ocean's physics is written and not computed. Each of ph/p1 to p6 states four strings (liminality, frequency, coupling, cache), and algos/geom.spw writes five formulas as nested lists; nothing in packages, scripts or src evaluates k_curvature, rho_density, e_energy or phase.entropy. The density formula reads today as a sheet term: nodes 12 and edges 30(2) give rho 0.227(15)."
 ocean_disagrees: "The prose disagrees with its source in one number: ph/p4.spw:20 gives the merge phase liminality 3, and docs/design/spw/spirit-sequence.spw:90 gives & liminality 2."
 sheet_beside_parser: "The SI constants sheet read under --si does not parse clean: 1 error. With the mol^-1 of %N_A[6.02214076e23 mol^-1] written /mol it has 0, and written mol^(-1) it still has 1, so the parser does not read a minus after ^; the sheet reads all three as one number. The floor sheets in the probes are written 90/s^2 for that reason and parse with 0 errors."
}

^"table"{
 # Counts, not prose. A cell is the number of pivots of that kind for which the column holds.
 corpus: "164 lines: 43 seed lines (babble/seed.spw and pivots.test.ts) and 121 real lines, the first of each shape among 642 short lines with pivots in 88 files of docs/theory/spw and .spw/biome/ocean. Real lines are trimmed of outer space and otherwise as written. 856 pivots."
 selection: "Of 12,382 lines in those files: 1,790 blank, 1,330 comments, 2,429 longer than 64 characters, 2,999 with a quote or a backtick, 2,190 with unbalanced braces, leaving 1,644."
 instrument: "A copy of pivots.ts that also records each pivot's site returns the same pivots as pivotsOf on 164 of 164 lines."

 # 1. What each kind conserves.
 conserved_columns: "kind | n | names | mark bag | mark count | wall bag | wall count | characters | ink count | ink bag | parser statements | spoken clauses"
 conserved_side: "side | 154 | 149 | 154 | 154 | 154 | 154 | 154 | 154 | 154 | 46 | 58"
 conserved_mark: "mark | 318 | 318 | 0 | 318 | 318 | 318 | 318 | 318 | 0 | 295 | 311"
 conserved_walls: "walls | 148 | 94 | 148 | 148 | 0 | 148 | 95 | 148 | 0 | 132 | 106"
 conserved_bond: "bond | 105 | 105 | 0 | 105 | 105 | 105 | 105 | 105 | 0 | 94 | 105"
 conserved_spacing: "spacing | 35 | 35 | 35 | 35 | 35 | 35 | 0 | 35 | 35 | 35 | 34"
 conserved_exchange: "exchange | 34 | 34 | 34 | 34 | 34 | 34 | 34 | 34 | 34 | 21 | 24"
 conserved_attach: "attach | 62 | 3 | 62 | 62 | 62 | 62 | 0 | 62 | 62 | 62 | 37"
 conserved_all: "all | 856 | 738 | 433 | 856 | 708 | 856 | 706 | 856 | 285 | 685 | 675"
 conserved_notes: "Ink is every character that is not a space; a bag is a multiset. Marks and walls are counted as characters as written, so a dot inside a name counts as a mark. Names are counted by readFragments. Statements moved: side 92 more, 9 fewer, 7 to prose; mark 12 more, 4 fewer; exchange 11 more. Clauses moved: side 82 fewer, 14 more; attach 25 fewer; walls 25 more, 17 fewer."

 # 2. Which kinds are their own reverse: does one pivot of the result write the exact line back.
 undone_columns: "kind | n | by the same kind | by another kind | by none | read by the line reader | same | other | none"
 undone_side: "side | 154 | 103 | 0 | 51 | 102 | 102 | 0 | 0"
 undone_mark: "mark | 318 | 303 | 0 | 15 | 301 | 301 | 0 | 0"
 undone_walls: "walls | 148 | 0 | 0 | 148 | 91 | 0 | 0 | 91"
 undone_bond: "bond | 105 | 105 | 0 | 0 | 105 | 105 | 0 | 0"
 undone_spacing: "spacing | 35 | 35 | 0 | 0 | 35 | 35 | 0 | 0"
 undone_exchange: "exchange | 34 | 19 | 2 | 13 | 28 | 19 | 2 | 7"
 undone_attach: "attach | 62 | 0 | 0 | 62 | 2 | 0 | 0 | 2"
 undone_notes: "All 15 mark turns that are not undone wrote a join mark (~ ^ & @); 80 other turns onto a join mark are undone. The 2 exchanges undone by another kind are undone by a side move (ba~~ba back to ~ba~ba)."

 # 3. Orbits: the same move at the same site, repeated. 5 lines with a repeated name left out.
 orbit_columns: "move | orbits | home in 2 | home in 3 | home in 4 | home in 12 | not home in 14 turns | move lost on the way"
 orbit_spacing: "spacing | 27 | 27 | 0 | 0 | 0 | 0 | 0"
 orbit_exchange: "exchange | 27 | 17 | 0 | 0 | 0 | 6 | 4"
 orbit_side_name: "side, marks on a name | 99 | 88 | 0 | 0 | 0 | 1 | 10"
 orbit_side_walls: "side, marks outside walls | 48 | 8 | 0 | 0 | 0 | 0 | 40"
 orbit_mark_name: "mark turned forward, on a name | 104 | 0 | 0 | 0 | 89 | 0 | 15"
 orbit_mark_walls: "mark turned forward, outside walls | 48 | 0 | 0 | 0 | 33 | 0 | 15"
 orbit_walls: "walls | 141 | 0 | 14 | 20 | 0 | 47 | 60"
 orbit_bond: "bond: each of the four join marks is one pivot from the other three, so there is no ring to walk"
 orbit_examples: "(x) to [x] to {x} to <x> and home in 4. =foo@(<bar>) to =foo@([bar]) to =foo@({bar}) and home in 3, the scene around it skipped. $%[catalog, Hold] to [catalog, Hold]%$, from which no side move is offered."

 # 4. Where the three readers part.
 readers_columns: "kind | n | line reader | parser | spoken | all three | line reader only | parser and spoken only | none | first failing check of the line reader: text left over | a name lost | fragment not where the pivot put it"
 readers_side: "side | 154 | 102 | 57 | 59 | 20 | 45 | 3 | 16 | 37 | 0 | 15"
 readers_mark: "mark | 318 | 301 | 297 | 252 | 233 | 2 | 2 | 2 | 2 | 0 | 15"
 readers_walls: "walls | 148 | 91 | 130 | 127 | 66 | 4 | 51 | 4 | 5 | 49 | 3"
 readers_bond: "bond | 105 | 105 | 99 | 96 | 90 | 0 | 0 | 0 | 0 | 0 | 0"
 readers_spacing: "spacing | 35 | 35 | 35 | 33 | 33 | 0 | 0 | 0 | 0 | 0 | 0"
 readers_exchange: "exchange | 34 | 28 | 21 | 32 | 17 | 0 | 3 | 1 | 1 | 0 | 5"
 readers_attach: "attach | 62 | 2 | 62 | 62 | 2 | 0 | 60 | 0 | 25 | 34 | 1"
 readers_all: "all | 856 | 664 | 701 | 661 | 461 | 51 | 119 | 23 | 70 | 83 | 39"
 side_columns: "side move | n | line reader | parser | spoken | all three | statements more | clauses fewer"
 side_down_name: "before to after, marks on a name | 93 | 81 | 37 | 6 | 3 | 51 | 82"
 side_down_walls: "before to after, marks outside walls | 47 | 7 | 6 | 39 | 3 | 41 | 0"
 side_up_name: "after to before, marks on a name | 13 | 13 | 13 | 13 | 13 | 0 | 0"
 side_up_walls: "after to before, marks outside walls | 1 | 1 | 1 | 1 | 1 | 0 | 0"

 # 5. Which pairs of kinds commute. A cell is equal / differ / second move no longer offered.
 commute_method: "A move is a kind, an address (a name, or a bond named by the names on its two sides, so it survives an exchange) and an action. 150 lines with no repeated name; 1,776 pairs of read pivots; 1,153 pairs with an unread pivot left out."
 commute_cross_total: "two different sites | 985 pairs | 945 / 26 / 14"
 commute_cross_clean: "no exception in 16 pairs of kinds: bond x mark 216, mark x walls 115, bond x side 72, mark x mark 72, mark x spacing 72, bond x walls 66, mark x side 46, bond x bond 45, side x walls 40, bond x spacing 30, side x spacing 24, spacing x walls 22, side x side 6, spacing x spacing 5, attach x walls 3, attach x mark 2"
 commute_cross_walls_walls: "walls x walls | 1 / 17 / 0 | x[a]{b}: wall a then wall b writes x<a>(b); wall b then wall a writes x<b>{a}"
 commute_cross_exchange_mark: "exchange x mark | 50 / 8 / 2 | @a*@b: exchange then turn a's mark writes b@@a=; turn then exchange writes b@#a*"
 commute_cross_exchange_side: "exchange x side | 18 / 1 / 1 | @a*@b*@c: exchange a and b then move b's mark writes @*b@a*@c; the other order writes *b@@a*@c"
 commute_cross_exchange_walls: "exchange x walls | 15 / 0 / 5 | x[@a*@b]: after the exchange (x[b@@a*]) a's wall turn is not offered; the other order writes x{b@@a*}"
 commute_cross_bond_exchange: "bond x exchange | 18 / 0 / 3 | a~b~c: after the outer exchange (c~a~b) the bond between a and b is no longer a bond of the line; the other order writes c~a^b"
 commute_cross_exchange_exchange: "exchange x exchange | 1 / 0 / 1 | a~b~c: outer then inner is not offered; inner (b~a~c) then outer writes c~b~a"
 commute_cross_exchange_spacing: "exchange x spacing | 6 / 0 / 1 | a~b~c: after the outer exchange (c~a~b) the inner bond is not there to space"
 commute_cross_attach_side: "attach x side | 0 / 0 / 1 | =a@(b): after the attach (=a@ (b)) the side move is not offered; side (a=@(b)) then attach writes a=@ (b)"
 commute_same_total: "one site | 791 pairs | 673 / 104 / 14"
 commute_same_clean: "no exception in 5 pairs of kinds: mark x side 207, mark x mark 190, mark x walls 107, bond x spacing 81, side x side 2"
 commute_same_bond_bond: "bond x bond | 0 / 81 / 0 | a^b: the last mark written stands, a&b or a~b; an overwrite, not an interaction"
 commute_same_bond_exchange: "bond x exchange | 51 / 12 / 3 | @a*@b: bond then exchange writes b~@a*; exchange then bond writes b@~a*"
 commute_same_exchange_spacing: "exchange x spacing | 17 / 4 / 1 | @a*@b: spacing then exchange writes b @ @a*; exchange then spacing writes b@ @ a*"
 commute_same_side_walls: "side x walls | 18 / 7 / 0 | =(a)@b: side (a)=@b then wall writes =[a]@b, the mark back in front; wall then side writes [a]=@b"
 commute_same_attach: "attach x bond 0 / 0 / 6, attach x exchange 0 / 0 / 2, attach x spacing 0 / 0 / 2 | =a@(b): bond then attach writes =a~ (b), exchange then attach writes (b)@ =a, and after the attach (=a@ (b)) there is no bond to turn, exchange or space; =a @ (b) offers no attach"
 commute_examples: "The example lines are short made lines found by the same script; the counts are from the corpus alone, and the corpus's own first counterexamples are in physics-scratch/commute.log."
 collisions: "two kinds writing one line | exchange and side | 2 | ~ba~ba: moving the first ~ after ba and exchanging the two sides both write ba~~ba"

 # 6. Pivots of a sheet's term lines: what happens to the term's quantity (13 term lines of dimensional-analysis.spw on the SI constants).
 sheet_columns: "kind | n | same quantity | same dimension, other value | other dimension | refused | term gone"
 sheet_side: "side | 21 | 0 | 0 | 0 | 8 | 13"
 sheet_mark: "mark | 48 | 0 | 0 | 0 | 22 | 26"
 sheet_walls: "walls | 19 | 0 | 0 | 0 | 6 | 13"
 sheet_bond: "bond | 42 | 0 | 0 | 0 | 42 | 0"
 sheet_spacing: "spacing | 14 | 6 | 0 | 0 | 8 | 0"
 sheet_exchange: "exchange | 14 | 0 | 0 | 2 | 12 | 0"
 sheet_attach: "attach | 28 | 20 | 0 | 0 | 8 | 0"
 sheet_all: "all | 186 | 26 | 0 | 2 | 106 | 52"
 sheet_examples: "%r_s[2*@G*@M_sun/@c^2] spaced to %r_s[2*@G*@M_sun/@c ^ 2] is the same quantity; exchanged across the power to %r_s[2^2*@G*@M_sun/@c] it reads L^2·T^-1 1.77078e+12 where it read L 2953.34."

 # 7. Pinch: the pendulum sheet under spw sheet --pi.
 pinch_columns: "how the pendulum is written | groups shown | values"
 pinch_si: "T 2.006 s, L 1 m, m 1 kg, g 9.81 m/s^2 | T^2 · L^-1 · g | 39.47579"
 pinch_units: "T 2006 ms, L 100 cm, m 1000 g, g 35.316 km/min^2 | T^2 · L^-1 · g | 39.47579"
 pinch_natural: "the first again under --natural c,hbar,G, where T reads 3.720846e+43 | T^2 · L^-1 · g | 39.47579"
 pinch_order: "the terms written g, m, L, T | g · L^-1 · T^2 | 39.47579"
 pinch_on_law: "L 4 m and T 4.012 s | T^2 · L^-1 · g | 39.47579"
 pinch_off_law: "L 4 m and T 2.006 s | T^2 · L^-1 · g | 9.868948"
 pinch_two: "an amplitude A 0.1 m added, written T, L, m, g, A | T^2 · L^-1 · g and L · A^-1 | 39.47579 and 10"
 pinch_two_reordered: "the same five written A, g, L, m, T | A · L^-1 and A · g^-1 · T^-2 | 0.1 and 0.002533198"
 pinch_floor: "spw.quest's floor from its source: k 90/s^2, damping rate 2*0.7*k^(1/2), step 1/60 s | k · damp^-2 and k · dt^2 | 0.5102041 and 0.025"
 pinch_floor_marks: "the floor's held body (k times 2.6) and drifting body (k times 0.3) | each k · damp^-2 | 0.5102041 and 0.5102041; natural periods 410.7447 ms and 1209.2 ms, plain 662.3059 ms"

 # 8. Derivative: the measured sheet's period, 2.0060667 s, against a finite difference.
 derivative_columns: "input | derivative of the period | nudge | period moved | derivative times nudge | ratio"
 derivative_rod: "L_rod 1.000(1) m | 1.0030333 | 0.001 | 1.002783e-3 | 1.003033e-3 | 0.999750"
 derivative_rod_far: "L_rod | 1.0030333 | 0.1 | 9.791380e-2 | 1.003033e-1 | 0.976177"
 derivative_g: "g_local 9.810(20) m/s^2 | -0.1022460 | 0.02 | -2.041799e-3 | -2.044920e-3 | 0.998474"
 derivative_g_far: "g_local | -0.1022460 | 2 | -1.777353e-1 | -2.044920e-1 | 0.869155"
 derivative_exact: "the same period from ^pendulum{ %L[1 m] %g[9.81 m/s^2] %period[2*pi*(@L/@g)^(1/2)] }, no uncertainty written | no derivative is kept: grad undefined, uncertainty 0"
 derivative_shown: "spw sheet --json gives si, uncertainty and dimension for each row; no flag or field gives the derivative by input"

 # 9. The dial against every order, opposition and grouping of marks found.
 dial_columns: "order of all twelve | where | dial half-turn pairs still a half turn apart | dial neighbours still neighbours"
 dial_lexer: "! ^ ~ ? * = @ # . & $ % | token.ts:17, act-chains.spw:16 and the runtime's type-affinities.ts:19-30 | the dial itself | the dial itself"
 dial_atlas: "? ! ^ ~ * = @ # . & $ % | operator-atlas.spw:21 | 2 of 6 | 9 of 12"
 dial_names: "~ # . ? ! * & @ ^ $ % = | operators.spw:28-40 | 0 of 6 | 2 of 12"
 dial_runtime: "# @ & = % $ . ? ! ^ ~ * | operators.spw:46-58 | 1 of 6 | 4 of 12"
 dial_strategies: "! ~ ? . ^ # @ = & * $ % | operators.spw:144-156 | 2 of 6 | 5 of 12"
 dial_effects: "* ~ ! ? @ = $ % # ^ . & | act-chains.spw:68-79 | 1 of 6 | 3 of 12"
 dial_quest: "~ ? ! * . ^ # @ & = % $ | spw.quest's guide.js:8-19 | 0 of 6 | 3 of 12"
 dial_ladders: "operator-ladders.spw points to form-ladders.spw, whose six ladders order the forms of a paired boundary and give the marks no order, opposition or grouping"
 opposition_columns: "pair | who states it | steps apart on the dial, where 6 is a half turn"
 opposition_ground_ascension: ". and ^ | factshift.center's canvas (settle +2.4, lift -2.4) and spw.quest's floor (6 px, -6 px) | 5"
 opposition_perspective_wonder: "@ and ? | the canvas (gather 0.04, open -0.03) and the floor (0.25, -0.25) | 3"
 opposition_potential_configuration: "~ and = | the canvas (a seat let go by half, or held again) | 3"
 opposition_value_potential: "* and ~ | the floor (stiff 2.6, stiff 0.3) and act-chains defer_commit | 2"
 opposition_act_prime: "! and ~ | act-chains prime_act and wonder_trial_prime_actualize | 2"
 opposition_address_measure: "$ and % | act-chains address_measure | 1"
 opposition_potentiate_vibrate: "~ (with ? and a bias =) and # | brace-charge-crawl.spw:190, potentiate against vibrate | 5 (4 and 2)"
 opposition_dial_six: "!@ ^# ~. ?& *$ =% | stated as an opposition by any host or surface found | 0 of 6"
 quarter_columns: "grouping | where | quarter 1 (! ^ ~) | quarter 2 (? * =) | quarter 3 (@ # .) | quarter 4 (& $ %)"
 quarter_containers: "the atlas's four containers | operator-atlas.spw:25-30 | none | ? | # . @ | none"
 quarter_transformers: "the atlas's seven transformers | operator-atlas.spw:33-41 | ! ~ ^ | * | none | % $ &"
 quarter_spirit: "the spirit sequence's six phases, in dial positions 3 2 6 9 4 1 | .spw/workspace.spw:83 | ~ ^ | ? * | @ | &"
 quarter_joins: "the four join marks | line/names.ts:50 | ~ ^ | none | @ | &"
 quarter_canvas_law: "marks with a body law on the canvas | local-forces.ts:41 | ^ ~ ! | * = ? | . @ | %"
 quarter_canvas_none: "marks the canvas gives no law | local-forces.ts:21 | none | none | # | & $"
 quarter_floor_law: "marks with a law on spw.quest's floor | physics.js:58-64 | ^ ~ ! | * ? | . @ | none"
 quarter_property: "the two marks the runtime gives one access mode, property | type-affinities.ts:24, :27 | none | = | . | none"
 ring_setting: "~soup turns to ?soup or ^soup under the dial, and to !soup or @soup under a ring that sets the hosts' three pairs a half turn apart (. @ ~ ! * # ^ ? = % $ &). .bed turns to &bed or #bed, and to @bed or &bed. Each comes home in 12 under either ring, and in 9 under the nine-ring of pivots.test.ts."

 # 10. Label scans (scanPairLabels). + is accumulate, - is release.
 label_columns: "line | pairs | crossings | tree | events forward | events backward"
 label_sequential: "{_A a }_A {_B b }_B | 2 | 0 | true | +A -A +B -B | +B -B +A -A"
 label_nested: "{_A a {_B b }_B }_A | 2 | 0 | true | +A +B -B -A | +A +B -B -A"
 label_crossed: "{_A a {_B b }_A c }_B | 2 | 1 | false | +A +B -A -B | +B +A -B -A"
 label_same: "{_A a {_A b }_A c }_A | 2 | 0 | true | +A +A -A -A | +A +A -A -A"
 label_six_events: "{_A a1 {_B b1 a2 b2 a3 }_A b3 }_B | 2 | 1 | false | +A +B -A -B | +B +A -B -A"
 label_n: "n pairs all crossed, n from 2 to 8 | n | 1, 3, 6, 10, 15, 21, 28 | false | as the pair by pair count in pair-labels.test.ts:234-248 implies"
 label_directions: "both directions return the same pairs and crossings on 15 of 15 lines, as wonder_trial_pair_label already records"
 label_pivots: "pivots of four labeled lines | 20 | keep pairs and crossings 16 | change them 4, all wall turns"
}

^"probes"{
 # babble/probe.mts on every line this report names, in the order named: parser | line reader | spoken reader | pivots and fragments. The median timing is left out; nothing else is edited.
