^"broken"{
 # The seed's babble claims in this lens, tested against the code and the counts above. First, for each of the five claims asked about: measurable today, or metaphor only.
 verdict_pinch: "Measurable today. spw sheet --pi gives the groups and their values; the value holds through any units by construction, and it separates a zoom along the law from one off it."
 verdict_derivative: "Measurable today in the library and not at the command line: Quantity.grad holds the derivative by input, for inputs written with an uncertainty only."
 verdict_dial: "Metaphor only as stated. No reader, host or surface computes or states a half-turn opposition or a quarter. What is measurable beside it: a ring is a setting whose turns come home in 12, and two hosts give marks signed forces that the dial does not follow."
 verdict_labels: "Partly measurable today. Created and annihilated are scanPairLabels' accumulate and release, counted and equal in a whole text, with crossings and a tree flag. Parallel time is metaphor: the scan counts overlap, not the order of events."
 verdict_rotated_frame: "Metaphor only as stated: no host or reader gives the side of a mark a height or a force. One measurable stand-in exists, how many readers still read a line after a mark changes side."
 dial_opposites: "Contradicted. No host or theory surface found states any of the dial's six half-turn pairs as an opposition (0 of 6). The oppositions that are stated with numbers sit 5, 3, 3 and 2 steps apart on it. The dial sets ground opposite potential; both hosts set ground opposite ascension."
 dial_quarters: "Weaker than stated. One quarter matches a grouping that exists: @ # . is the atlas's four containers without ?. The quarter & $ % is where the forces run out: the canvas gives # & $ no law and spw.quest's floor gives none of & $ %. The other two quarters match nothing found."
 dial_order: "The order is the lexer's type union reused as the fallback for turns; no half turn or quarter in it was arranged. A ring is an option of pivotsOf (pivots.ts:119-122), and the same lines come home in 12 under a ring made from the hosts' oppositions."
 quadrants_rotation: "Weaker than stated. A wall turn returns in four only when all four pairs are free: 20 of 141 orbits. 14 return in three, 47 never write the starting line again, 60 lose the move, and no wall turn is undone by one pivot (0 of 148). operational-topography.spw:173 keeps the word rotation for a transform whose inverse is defined."
 quadrants_one_per_seat: "Holds, and more strongly than stated: one wall kind per seat is enforced, which is why two walls of one word do not commute (17 of 18)."
 label_must_cross: "False as written. Two streams on one line cross only when each opens inside the other and closes outside it; written one after the other, or one inside the other, they have 0 crossings."
 label_only_crossing: "Weaker than stated. A label is the only brace that crosses the tree, and a reference crosses it too: depiction-frames.spw:71 calls @name a sight line across frames and spw.quest's floor draws one (physics.js:15), as in garden{ bed{seed: water} @well }."
 label_vertices: "Weaker than stated. A crossing is one vertex for each two overlapping spans however many events interleave, so tracks with vertices show that two streams overlap and not the order of what happens inside the overlap."
 names_law: "Weaker than the seed's note that names are already a law: it is true of the pivots shown with a reading and false of the pivots offered: 118 of 856 change the names, 69 of them losing one."
 pinch_groups: "Holds for units, by construction. Weaker for what a reader sees: the groups shown depend on the order the terms are written (39.47579 and 10 become 0.1 and 0.002533198). What survives is how many groups there are and the space they span."
 gestures_pinch: "Holds in one measured sense: the two pivot kinds the seed gives to pinch, spacing and attach, are the only kinds under which a sheet term keeps its quantity (26 of 42, against 0 of 144)."
 gestures_one_change: "Not true of the wall turn as built. One turn also strips inner padding (53 of 148 lines get shorter), changes more than the two wall characters in 9 (a word's slots reordered, or a mark outside the walls moved), and writes a mark that stood after the walls back in front of them (side x walls differs in 7 of 25)."
 derivative_per_step: "Weaker than stated. Only a number written with an uncertainty carries a derivative (sheet.ts:171); the pendulum sheet's own numbers carry none. It is first order: 2.4 per cent short at a 10 per cent step in L, 13 per cent at a 20 per cent step in g. The CLI shows the combined uncertainty and never the derivative."
 evaluation_is_a_pivot: "Contradicted for sheets and the seven kinds as built. No pivot of a term line moves its quantity to a nearby value (0 of 186): a pivot leaves the quantity alone or breaks the term. An evaluation step replaces a name with a value, and every read pivot keeps every name."
 rotated_frame_top: "Weaker than stated. Both hosts already have an up and a down, set by the mark and not by the side: ascension rests high and ground rests low. Potential is not on that axis on either host; there it is looseness. Neither host gives a mark after a name any law (physics.js:10 reads a body's leading mark; local-forces.ts:44-45 takes a word's first character)."
 rotated_frame_gravity: "Has measurable content, and it points the other way. If height is how many readers still read a line, before the name is the low ground today: a mark moved after its name is read by all three readers in 6 of 140 cases, and a mark moved back in 14 of 14."
}

^"wonders"{
 # Open wonders, each an experiment someone could run on a canvas: what a hand does, what is conserved, what they would see. Prior art first; only what is new is asked.
 three_counters: "Prior art: wonder_trial_field_order asks what is conserved, what has a sign and whether effects add, and says nothing measured is conserved the way charge is; depiction-frames.spw:75 lists the line's bytes. New: three counts no pivot changes. The hand: on =foo@(<bar>) turn a mark, turn a wall, exchange the two sides. Conserved: ink 12, marks 2, walls 4, through all 11 pivots. Seen: three counters that never move beside three reader lights that flicker, and two kinds of move (a wall turn, an attach) drawn as arrows with no way back. Would a counter that stays still teach more than a force that always moves?"
 four_seats: "Prior art: the seed's quadrants babble, and the D4 note in brace-physics.spw:297, a proposed visualization. New: the seats exclude. The hand: on x[a]{b} twist a's wall and then b's; put the line back; twist b's and then a's. Conserved: three names, four wall characters. Seen: x<a>(b) one way and x<b>{a} the other, because a seat already taken is skipped. Is a wall turn the rotation of one wall, or a move in a game of four seats where the order of play shows?"
 reader_slope: "Prior art: act-chains.spw:60 reads side by arms; the seed's trailing and pivots_foo notes and pivots.test.ts:61-63 already say a mark after a name reads in the line reader only; pivotReadCounts counts acceptance for postfix. New: the split by direction over a corpus, 140 moves down and 14 up. The hand: with the frame turned a quarter, drag the ^ of ^sky{sun, rain} from above the name to below it, and back. Conserved: every character. Seen: one light for each reader; going down all three go out (sky^{sun, rain}: the line reader reads ^ as a bond, the parser makes two statements, the spoken reader says sky, ascension, definition), and from there no pivot leads back; dragged back by hand, all three light again. Is the slope a fact about the language, or about what today's readers were never asked to read?"
 one_motion_three_clocks: "Prior art: dimensional-analysis.spw's groups and its wonder on unit systems; wonder_trial_modality on whether a force is a reading or a decoration. New: a host's feel written as a sheet. The hand: on spw.quest's floor with pantry{rice, oats, ~jar{salt, honey}, *tin{tea}}, push a part of the jar and a part of the tin the same distance and let go. Conserved: the damping group, 0.5102041, by construction. Seen: the same curve home on two clocks, the jar's 2.94 times slower than the tin's, and a pinch along time that lays one over the other. Would a reader told that * and ~ are one motion at two speeds find the two marks easier to tell apart, or harder?"
 label_tracks: "Prior art: wonder_trial_pair_label and wonder_trial_inside (spans, coverage, both scan directions agree); the pair sound table gives a label a timbre. New: the drag as an experiment, and what a pivot does to a label. The hand: on {_A a {_B b }_B }_A drag the close of A leftward past the close of B. Conserved: 2 pairs, 2 opens, 2 closes. Seen: one vertex appears and the tree light goes out ({_A a {_B b }_A c }_B); the same drag between two A labels changes nothing, since the nearer close pairs with the nearer open; a wall turn on a labeled body makes its pair vanish. Is the number of vertices the thing worth hearing, more than the order of the clicks?"
}

^"unverified"{
 hosts_from_source: "The floor's and the canvas's numbers were read from the site consumer's working tree and not run; the floor's stiffness and damping rate were worked out from physics.js:267 and physics.js:282. Whether the deployed pages match that tree was not checked."
 corpus_scope: "The counts hold for short, unquoted, brace-balanced lines; 2,999 lines with a quote and 2,429 longer than 64 characters were left out, and each real shape counts once however many lines share it (the anchor shape #>name stands for 214 lines)."
 commutation_scope: "Commutation was measured where both pivots were read; 1,153 pairs with an unread pivot and 5 lines with a repeated name were left out."
 dialects: "Every parser count is under the default dialect. The seed's note that 15 pivot lines read alike under all eight dialects was not re-run."
 one_ring: "Orbits were walked under the default ring; two other rings were tried on three lines only."
 why_the_order: "That ACT_MARKS was copied from the lexer's union, and not both from a third place, is inferred from their being identical; no history was read."
 opposition_reading: "Calling two marks opposed because one branch of a host's code gives them opposite signs is this report's reading of local-forces.ts and physics.js, not a statement by either host's author."
 recall: "The seed's from_recall items were not checked, and nothing here rests on them."
 opposition_sweep: "The search for stated oppositions read the surfaces the task named and searched docs/theory/spw, docs/design/spw, .spw/registries and .spw/workspace.spw for opposite, dual, polar, inverse, complement, pole, mirror, counterpart, versus and arrows between two marks. A pairing written in other words, or in a consumer's plans, would have been missed, so 0 of 6 is a count of what was found."
 upward_n: "After to before was measured on 14 moves, against 140 the other way."
 not_reached: "The curvature and hyperbolic babble; field-dynamics, whose surface names four conservation tests of field.ts that were neither read nor run here; the phasor surface, which names three layers as phase angles and has no number today."
}

^"sources"{
 pivots: "packages/spw-seed/src/experimental/pivots.ts:48 (ACT_MARKS), :50 (the wall turn's order), :119-122 (a host's order), :258-265 (read-back and the status), :311-317 (walls), :330-339 (attach); pivots.test.ts:79-86 (names kept on five lines), :88-94 (a host's ring)"
 line_names: "packages/spw-seed/src/line/names.ts:50 (the four join marks)"
 lexer_order: "packages/spw-seed/src/types/token.ts:17 (OperatorKind); packages/spw-runtime/src/state/type-affinities.ts:19-30 (the same order, with an access mode for each)"
 sheet: "packages/spw-seed/src/experimental/physics/dimension.ts:48 (scale in SI base units), :55 (grad), :134-136 (pure and measured); sheet.ts:57 (uncertainty), :171 (a derivative only for a number with an uncertainty); analysis.ts:36-40 (groups from the null space); constants.ts:18 (mol^-1); packages/spw-cli/src/sheet.ts:127-131 (what a row shows)"
 labels: "packages/spw-seed/src/experimental/pair-labels.ts:248 (scanBraceEdges), :279 (scanPairLabels); pair-labels.test.ts:112-116, :218, :234-248; .agents/plans/pair-label-reading/wip.spw:57 (a label makes a class)"
 theory: "docs/theory/spw/act-chains.spw:16, :60, :63, :68-79, :84-87; operators.spw:28-40, :46-58, :96-101, :144-156; operator-atlas.spw:21, :25-30, :33-41; operator-ladders.spw:14-18 and form-ladders.spw:41-67; brace-charge-crawl.spw:170-190; dimensional-analysis.spw:36-66; operational-topography.spw:92, :173; depiction-frames.spw:71, :75; threshold-distance.spw:106; docs/design/spw/spirit-sequence.spw:20-27, :86-92; .spw/workspace.spw:83; .spw/registries/brace-physics.spw:13, :297"
 ocean: ".spw/biome/ocean/ph/p1.spw:19-24 and the same facet in p2 to p6 (four strings each); ph/p4.spw:20; algos/geom.spw:13-36 (five formulas as lists); algos/material.spw; packages/spw-lsp/src/handlers/display.ts:630 (the one place a phase measure is named, as a label)"
 trials: ".agents/plans/interpretation-trials/interpretation-trials.spw:529 (modality), :630 (joint and sight line), :699 (turn), :788 (pair label), :921 (inside), :939 (field order), :958 (scales)"
 spw_quest: "the site consumer workers/spw-quest/src/physics.js:10, :15 (the floor's rules), :41 (the pantry line), :56 (feel), :58-64 (seven laws), :267, :282 (the spring and its damping); guide.js:8-19 (operator order)"
 canvas: "the site consumer workers/factshift-center/app/src/ts/simulation/local-forces.ts:12-21, :29-38, :41, :44-45, :72-99; app/src/js/modes/spw/body-gestures.ts:41-42 (pinch thresholds), :77-87 (what each law is said to do)"
 scratch: "babble/physics-scratch: corpus.mts, make-inst.mts, lib.mts, measure.mts, commute.mts, commute-min.mts, verify.mts, side-arrow.mts, names-direction.mts, sheet-physics.mts, si-check.mts, dial.mts, labels.mts, gen-probes.mts, and a .log beside each; cite-lines.txt holds the probed lines"
}
